-----------
without MSYS2
-----------
IDE's like CLion don't support MSYS and therefore no posix shell.
download mingw32 or 64
https://github.com/niXman/mingw-builds-binaries/releases
expand assets and download/unpack
download or git clone denise
in the following we need to include more headers / libraries to our mingw installation folder.
the first include / lib folders you see in mingw main folder are NOT the target folders,
therefore change to subfolder: x86_64-w64-mingw32 (64 bit) or i686-w64-mingw32 (32 bit)
from denise folder
  copy: data/libs/static/win(32)64/libfreetype.a to mingw lib folder
  copy: data/libs/include/ft2build.h to mingw include folder
  copy folder with contents: data/libs/include/freetype to mingw include folder

open a cmd:
  we need to set mingw 32 or 64 bit to system environment variables
  input: set Path=<mingw_path>\mingw(32)64\bin;%Path%
  replace <mingw_path> with your specific mingw installation path
  i recommend to rename 'bin\mingw32-make.exe' to 'make.exe'

in denise root folder
make SubSystem=win32
make SubSystem=win32 install
